**What I deliberately left to the magistrate**

The handback assigns the harvest, the uninstall from the clone and the plan-root retirement to the relaunched magistrate, and only after the 03:45 completion boundary with courier.sent present. The watchdog's span logic releases the span at that boundary, so it can relaunch the magistrate at its first tick after 03:45. Running the uninstall from here would act before that boundary and risk two agents retiring the same root, so no uninstall was attempted and no retained or UNKNOWN outcome exists. Both night plists remain installed until the magistrate's uninstall exits 0.

Nothing new is armed. This courier process exits now so it stops appearing in the census.
